or Non-Majors\nMaster of Science in Computational Linguistics\n5-year Bachelor's/Master's Program\nAdvising Frequently Asked Questions\nAdmissions Requirements\nLearning Goals\nHandbook and New Student Info\nMaster's Student Awards\nPhD Program\nDoctorate in Computer Science (PhD)\nRequirements\nLearning Goals\nDissertations\nCurrent PhD Students\nPhD Student Awards\nCourses\nResearch and Innovation\nResearch Labs\nRecent Results\nInnovation Resources\nPeople\nFaculty and Staff\nCurrent PhD Students\nCurrent COSI Master's Students\nWhere Are Our Alumni?\nCareer Guide\nNews and Events\nCalendar\nIn the News\nSpeaker Series\nContact Us\nHome\nAcademics\nSchools\nDegree Programs\nBrandeis Online\nSummer Programs\nMicrocredentials\nAdmissions & Aid\nUndergraduate Admissions\nGraduate Admissions\nFinancial Aid\nRabb School of Continuing Studies\nResearch\nCenters and Institutes\nFunding Resources\nAthletics\nStudent Life\nHousing/Community Living\nDining\nClubs and Organizations\nCommunity Service\nAthletics\nArts\nRose Art Museum\nAbout\nOur Story\nOur Jewish Roots\nMission and Diversity Statements\nFast Facts\nVisiting\nAdministration\nVisit\nStudents\nFaculty & Staff\nAlumni & Friends\nParents & Families\nGiving\nPopular Resources\nCampus Calendar\nDirectories\nEmployment\nMoodle\nNews/Media\nShuttle Schedules\nSupport at Brandeis\nWorkday\nSites A-Z\nMichtom School of Computer Science\nHome /\nPhD Program /\nRequirements\nRequirements\nCourse Requirements\nThe minimum degree requirements include an approved schedule of nine courses numbers 100 or above.\nThere is a three-year residency requirement for PhD students.\nAdviser\nBy the end of the first year, students must obtain the consent of a computer science faculty member to serve as adviser and dissertation committee chair.\nTeaching Requirement\nThe mentoring, training and evaluation of teaching fellows is an ongoing and important component of the graduate program. Students normally teach one course per semester, beginning as graders of problem sets and assignments, then move progressively to higher levels of involvement with teaching in courses across the curriculum. They participate in the design and delivery of course lectures and each year, under the guidance of their faculty, they present several lectures. Whether students are preparing for an academic and research career or an industry position, the teaching fellow experience is valuable training in course preparation and technical communication.\nThesis Committee and Proposal\nEstablishment by the adviser and the director of graduate studies of a thesis committee consisting of the adviser, two other Brandeis faculty and one appropriate external member from outside Brandeis.\nAn approved, written thesis proposal by the candidate that surveys the relevant literature and states the goals of the dissertation and topics to be investigated (including aspects already completed or underway), along with an oral presentation to the thesis committee that is open to computer science faculty who wish to attend.\nThesis Defense\nPublic defense of a completed dissertation will be announced three weeks in advance. Copies of the complete thesis will be available to the faculty during these three weeks.\nResidency Requirement\nYou can find out more about application requirements on the Graduate Admissions website. The minimum residency requirement is three years.\nUndergraduate Programs\nMaster's Programs\nPhD Program\nDoctorate in Computer Science (PhD)\nRequirements\nLearning Goals\nDissertations\nCurrent PhD Students\nPhD Student Awards\nCourses\nResearch and Innovation\nPeople\nCareer Guide\nNews and Events\nContact Us\nHome\nPhD Handbook (pdf)\nExplore Our Programs\nBachelor of Arts and Bachelor of Science\nMaster of Science\nMaster of Science for Non-Majors\nMaster of Science in Computational Linguistics\nPhD in Computer Science\nApply to Brandeis\nUndergraduate Admissions\nGraduate Admissions\nContact Us\nMichtom School of Computer Science\nVolen 261, MS 018\nBrandeis University\n415 South Street\nWaltham, MA 02453\n781-736-2700\ncompsci@brandeis.edu\nAbout Our Department\nThe Department of Computer Science is small enough to provide interactive and engaging learning with professors who are leading scholars and researchers in their fields, yet large enough to access resources that provide students with top-rate educational and research opportunities.\nBrandeis University\n\u00a92026\nAll rights reserved.\nUniversity Policies\nAccessibility Statement\nPrivacy\nEmergency Services", "links": [["Skip to content", "https://www.brandeis.edu/computer-science/phd/requirements.html#skip-content"], ["", "https://www.brandeis.edu"], ["Undergraduate Programs", "https://www.brandeis.edu/computer-science/undergraduate/index.html"], ["", "https://www.brandeis.edu/computer-science/phd/requirements.html"], ["Bachelor of Arts and Bachelor of Science in Computer Science", "https://www.brandeis.edu/computer-science/undergraduate/index.html"], ["Academic Advising", "https://www.brandeis.edu/computer-science/undergraduate/academic-advising.html"], ["Learning Goals", "https://www.brandeis.edu/registrar/bulletin/provisional/courses/subjects/1400.html#learninggoals"], ["Requirements", "https://www.brandeis.edu/computer-science/undergraduate/requirements.html"], ["Student FAQs", "https://www.brandeis.edu/computer-science/undergraduate/advising-faqs.html"], ["Computer Science Placement", "https://www.brandeis.edu/computer-science/undergraduate/placement.html"], ["Study Abroad", "https://www.brandeis.edu/computer-science/undergraduate/abroad.html"], ["5-year Bachelor's/Master's Program", "https://www.brandeis.edu/computer-science/undergraduate/bachelor-master.html"], ["Undergraduate Awards", "https://www.brandeis.edu/computer-science/undergraduate/student_awards.html"], ["Undergraduate Departmental Representatives", "https://www.brandeis.edu/computer-science/undergraduate/udr-reps.html"], ["Senior Honors Thesis", "ht